      "position": 0,
      "content": "CSUF General Transfer Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "61836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "ABOUT THIS MAJOR",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "63836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) The Bachelor of Arts in American Studies ( Link ) is an interdisciplinary study of the United States in the past and present. Courses focus on the cultural history of topics such as: race, immigration and ethnicity; gender, sexuality and body politics; popular culture, technology and the arts; work and leisure; the environment, communities and region; sports and mental health; film, literature and creative work; childhood and adolescence; and crime and violence. The program develops analytical thinking, reading and writing skills and fosters a critical engagement with the past and present, preparing students for careers in business, communications, government service, law, social services and teaching. An American Studies B.A. is an ideal double major and complements majors in Art, Communications, Criminal Justice, English, Ethnic Studies, History, Human Services, Liberal Studies, Music, Psychology, Sociology, and Women’s and Gender Studies. In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information. Students may take all 24 units in American Studies or select up to 12 units upper-division courses from a related field in consultation with an academic adviser. Electives may be used to explore an area of interest, such as race and ethnicity, law and society, gender roles, urbanization, technology, education, the child and the family, or popular culture. Consult with an adviser to help develop a plan that best fits your interests. AMST 101, AMST 131, AMST 132 or an adviser-approved AMST 100-level course may substitute for one 300-level course",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120 UNITS)</strong></p><p>The Bachelor of Arts in American Studies (<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47140&amp;returnto=15147\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>) is an interdisciplinary study of the United States in the past and present. Courses focus on the cultural history of topics such as: race, immigration and ethnicity; gender, sexuality and body politics; popular culture, technology and the arts; work and leisure; the environment, communities and region; sports and mental health; film, literature and creative work; childhood and adolescence; and crime and violence. The program develops analytical thinking, reading and writing skills and fosters a critical engagement with the past and present, preparing students for careers in business, communications, government service, law, social services and teaching. An American Studies B.A. is an ideal double major and complements majors in Art, Communications, Criminal Justice, English, Ethnic Studies, History, Human Services, Liberal Studies, Music, Psychology, Sociology, and Women’s and Gender Studies.</p><p><br></p><p>In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=101&amp;navoid=15099\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree</a>&nbsp;section in this catalog for complete information.</p><p><br></p><p>Students may take all 24 units in American Studies or select up to 12 units upper-division courses from a related field in consultation with an academic adviser. Electives may be used to explore an area of interest, such as race and ethnicity, law and society, gender roles, urbanization, technology, education, the child and the family, or popular culture. Consult with an adviser to help develop a plan that best fits your interests.</p><p><br></p><p>AMST 101,&nbsp;AMST 131,&nbsp;AMST 132&nbsp;or an adviser-approved AMST 100-level course may substitute for one 300-level course</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "65836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Transfer Success Pathway major eligible",
      "contentHtml": "<p><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/transfer-success-pathway.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Success Pathway</a> major eligible </p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "b8a730af-af06-4545-b0d0-019d68d6b5af",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The information provided here is subject to change without notice. Please be advised that articulation agreements published here may be updated or added at any time. Be sure to check with a counselor or adviser for the most current requirements. For additional transfer information: For C-ID information: https://c-idsystem.org/courses/ For Common Course Numbering: https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/",
      "contentHtml": "<p></p><p></p><p><strong><em>The&nbsp;information&nbsp;provided&nbsp;here&nbsp;is&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;without&nbsp;notice.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;be&nbsp;advised&nbsp;that&nbsp;articulation&nbsp;agreements&nbsp;published&nbsp;here&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;updated&nbsp;or&nbsp;added&nbsp;at&nbsp;any&nbsp;time.&nbsp;Be&nbsp;sure&nbsp;to&nbsp;check&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;counselor&nbsp;or&nbsp;adviser&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;current&nbsp;requirements.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>For&nbsp;additional&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;information:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>For&nbsp;C-ID&nbsp;information:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://c-idsystem.org/courses/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://c-idsystem.org/courses/</a></li><li>For&nbsp;Common&nbsp;Course&nbsp;Numbering:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/</a></li></ul>"
